 "rulebook": "FIVB Official Volleyball Rules 2025-2028: Rule 1 (the court 18 m x 9 m, the front zone between the centre line and the attack line 3 m from it), Rule 2 (the men's net, top at 2.43 m, the antennas), Rule 3 (the ball: 65-67 cm round, 260-280 g), Rule 9.2 (the hit: not caught or thrown, one contact), Rule 11 (no contact with the net, the foot not wholly beyond the centre line)",
 "deviations": [
  "The pass is a scripted launch: a ball tossed without spin from the back court, the same in every attempt, instead of a team-mate.",
  "Rule 9.2 (the overhead pass with the fingers): the robot has no fingers, so the set is one contact of the hands (the parts beyond the wrists) with the ball's centre above the top of the robot's head (0.76 m above its waist joint along the trunk, about 1.80 m when it stands). 'Not caught or thrown' is a contact of at most 0.1 s (the ball cannot be gripped).",
  "A set is judged by numbers instead of a referee's eye: the ball must leave the hands moving upward and at least 1.0 times as fast as it arrived (hands held still in the ball's path return it at no more than three quarters of its speed: that is a rebound, not a set); it must be played after it has passed its highest point, by a setter who has stayed in the front zone.",
  "Nobody attacks the set: a good set is defined as volleyball coaching grades it, a ball that rises at least 1.0 m above the net and comes down in the outside hitter's target, a circle of 1.0 m radius at position 4, judged where the ball first touches the floor.",
  "No team-mates or opponents, no wind."
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Set the pass: with one overhead contact of your hands, send the volleyball that comes down above you at least a metre above the net and into the outside hitter's target along the net.",
  "rules": "You are the setter on an official volleyball court (9.0 m by 9.0 m on each side of the net; the net's top 2.43 m high). You stand in your front zone facing along the net: the net is 1.0 m to your right, the attack line 3.0 m from the centre line to your left, the side line of position 2 3.0 m behind you, the side line of position 4 ahead of you. A volleyball (0.21 m across, 0.27 kg, in air) is tossed to you from the back court 3.0 s after the start and comes down above you. The set is the ball's first contact after the toss, before it touches the floor: with your hands (the parts beyond the wrists; one or both), overhead (the ball's centre above the top of your head, which is 0.76 m above your waist joint along the trunk), after the ball has passed its highest point, all contacts within 0.1 s, over when the ball has been clear of you for 0.03 s. It must be a set, not a rebound: the ball leaves your hands moving upward and at least 1.0 times as fast as it was just before they touched it. Then the ball's centre must rise at least 1.0 m above the net's top, and the ball must come down in the outside hitter's target: its first contact with the floor is inside a circle of 1.0 m radius whose centre is 1.0 m from the net on your side and 1.0 m inside the side line ahead of you. That is the success. You fail if the ball touches the floor before your set, if any part of you other than a hand touches the ball, if the ball's centre is not above the top of your head when your hands first touch it, if you touch it before it has passed its highest point, if the contacts last longer than 0.1 s (the ball held), if the ball leaves your hands downward or slower than that, if you touch the ball again, if it does not rise that high or comes down outside the target, if before your set your pelvis is farther from the net than the attack line (you left the front zone), if you touch the net, an antenna or a post, if a foot of yours is on the floor wholly beyond the centre line, if you fall (your pelvis lower than 0.35 m above the floor, or any part of you other than the feet on the floor), or after 10 s. The ball cannot be gripped, and it cannot be touched while it waits to be tossed.",
  "venue": "You face +x, along the net, which is 1 m to your right; the back court is to your left. The ball waits 0.9 m above the floor in the back court, 5.5 m to your left and 1.5 m ahead of you. About 3 s after the start it is tossed; it climbs to about 3.8 m and comes down steeply (about 56 degrees below the horizontal) at just under 7 m/s, travelling from your left to your right. About 1.36 s after the toss it is 2.1 m above the floor about 0.25 m in front of your head; untouched it lands beside the centre line to your right. The hitter's target is painted on the floor 5 m ahead of you.",
  "difficulty": "The hands (rubber fists) have to meet a 7 m/s ball above the head and drive it away faster than it came, up to nearly 4 m and 5 m along the net into a 2 m circle, in a contact of a few hundredths of a second: the angle and the speed both have to be right, and arms that are only held up return the ball too slowly."
 },
